From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:33:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): copy a host config and paste it into Add host
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setting up the same hosts on another device meant entering every
connection, password, name, color and icon again.

Settings → host → Share now copies this host, or every saved host, as a
host config: one line of JSON with each host's connections, password,
name, color, badge display and icon. Pasting it into Add host → Paste
pairing link shows which hosts it adds or updates, and Import saves
them. A saved host keeps its other connections. Routed connections are
left out, since the daemon that routes them registers them again.

Fork-Change: F-18
